(Precise calcium-to-spike inference using biophysical generative models) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This Figshare repository is in support of "Precise calcium-to-spike inference using biophysical) Tj T*
(generative models" from Broussard et al. It contains the data exports, MATLAB plotting functions, Python) Tj T*
(plotting scripts, shared utilities, and rendered table assets used to reproduce the manuscript figures) Tj T*
(and supplementary figures.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Figure panels are generated by scripts in the matching figure* or supp_figure* directory. MATLAB panels) Tj T*
(are generally script-style functions named for the figure and panel range. Python panels are installable) Tj T*
(console entry points defined in setup.py.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Environment and paths) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Use MATLAB for .m scripts and a conda or venv Python environment for .py scripts. From the repository) Tj T*
(root on a Windows machine:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(python -m venv .venv) Tj T*
(.\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(pip install -e .) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Conda works equivalently after activating the target environment. Python entry points resolve data and) Tj T*
(output paths back to this project checkout, not to the environment's site-packages directory. If) Tj T*
(launching from an unusual working directory, set GCAMP_FIGSHARE_ROOT or FIGSHARE_PROJECT_DIR to the) Tj T*
(repository root.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For MATLAB, run scripts from the repository root or from their figure directory after adding the) Tj T*
(repository and Utilities to the MATLAB path. Outputs are written to the figure directory or its output) Tj T*
(subdirectory when saving is enabled.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Main figure contents) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- figure1: jGCaMP response properties. Panels cover single-spike responses, response) Tj T*
(  amplitude/kinetic summaries, paired-pulse and multi-spike response behavior, and jGCaMP8f in vivo) Tj T*
(  quiescent-event examples with last-aligned averages and fast decay summaries.) Tj T*
(- figure2: stopped-flow and bouton kinetic measurements across GCaMP variants. Scripts plot on/off) Tj T*
(  kinetics, stopped-flow rise times, bouton rise comparisons, Hill-style summaries, 10-pulse) Tj T*
(  responses, decay summaries, and kinetic contribution analyses.) Tj T*
(- figure3: biophysical generative model fits and spike-inference examples. MATLAB scripts show) Tj T*
(  stopped-flow and bouton/state fits for GCaMP6f, jGCaMP7f, and jGCaMP8f. The Python script compares) Tj T*
(  biophysical and linear SMC inference on simulated excitatory/inhibitory examples.) Tj T*
(- figure4: spike-inference performance on jGCaMP8f data. MATLAB scripts plot example) Tj T*
(  continuous/discrete spike predictions and correlation versus smoothing width for excitatory and) Tj T*
(  inhibitory cells using correlation_tbl_jG8f.mat. The Python script plots matched bias/recall-style) Tj T*
(  distributions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Supplementary figure contents) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- supp_figure1: saturation, elongation, and related controls for jGCaMP8f multi-spike protocols.) Tj T*
(- supp_figure2: EGTA/BAPTA clamp comparisons, including data and simulations for OGB and jGCaMP8f.) Tj T*
(- supp_figure3: magnesium and ionic-strength effects on steady-state fluorescence and kinetics) Tj T*
(  across sensors.) Tj T*
(- supp_figure4: stopped-flow decay traces, biexponential fits, and decay-component summaries.) Tj T*
(- supp_figure5: clustered parameter-set summaries used during GCaMP model parameter selection.) Tj T*
(- supp_figure6: model fits and model-state plots using the parameter JSON files stored with Table 3.) Tj T*
(- supp_figure9: legacy/additional jGCaMP8f correlation analyses. Current Figure 4 analyses use) Tj T*
(  figure4/correlation_tbl_jG8f.mat.) Tj T*
(- supp_figure10: example high/low SNR spike predictions and discrete spike timing metrics.) Tj T*
(- supp_figure11: STA/SNA bias and uncertainty distributions for matched or unmatched jGCaMP8f) Tj T*
(  detections. Run with run_supp_figure11_A_code.) Tj T*
(- supp_figure12: trialwise jGCaMP8f analyses using packaged CSV/NPZ exports. Run with) Tj T*
(  run_supp_figure12_code; the script writes the raincloud panel and combined trace panels only.) Tj T*
(- supp_figure13: jGCaMP8f Janelia-parameter comparison. suppfigure13_A_B_code.m uses) Tj T*
(  janelia_model_selection_data_jG8f.mat; run_supp_figure13_C_D_code plots trace and correlation-vs-) Tj T*
(  sigma comparisons.) Tj T*
(- supp_figure14: jGCaMP8m analyses. suppfigure14_A_B_C_code.m uses decay_v_spikeNum.mat for) Tj T*
(  quiescent binning; suppfigure14_D_E_code.m uses janelia_model_selection_data_jG8m.mat;) Tj T*
(  run_supp_figure14_F_G_code plots trace and correlation-vs-sigma comparisons.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Table1, Table2, Table3, and Table4 contain CSV, TeX, PDF, and render scripts for manuscript tables.) Tj T*
(Table1 contains the spike inference precision, recall, F-score, accuracy, bias, and uncertainty summary.) Tj T*
(Table3 contains the GCaMP kinetic parameter table and the JSON parameter files also used by) Tj T*
(supp_figure6. The PowerShell table render helpers regenerate TeX from the CSV inputs before compiling) Tj T*
(PDFs and require pdflatex; Python-backed helpers should be run from an activated environment or passed) Tj T*
(the appropriate Python executable where supported.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
